      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "P'AN Ch'êng-chang 潘檉章 (T. 聖木, H. 力田), d. July 1, 1663, age 38 (sui), historian, was a native of Wu-chiang, Kiangsu. Refraining from taking the examinations under the newly established Manchu regime, he and Wu Yen [q. v.] determined in 1652 to collaborate on a history of the Ming dynasty and on an historical account of the same period in poetical form.",
          "source": "eccp-3649313",
